# References

**Applications & Inspiration:**

* **Netflix** – Major influence on the core cinematic UI/UX design, dark-mode glassmorphism aesthetics, and horizontal scrolling content carousels.
* **Discord** – Core inspiration for the Party Hub's real-time voice chat, text messaging, and synchronized social room architecture.
* **TikTok / Instagram Reels** – Shaped the design and functional flow of the vertical 9:16 'Clips' community interface.

**Development Tools:**

* **Visual Studio Code** - Primary Integrated Development Environment (IDE)
* **Git & GitHub** - Version control and repository collaboration
* **Postman** - REST API testing, payload verification, and endpoint documentation
* **Docker** - Containerization of the client and server environments utilizing `docker-compose`

**Libraries & Frameworks:**

* **React.js (v19)** - Primary declarative frontend user interface library
* **Vite** - High-performance frontend build engine and development bundler
* **Express.js** - Backend web application framework for Node.js
* **Socket.IO** - Bidirectional real-time event routing engine for synchronized playback
* **Firebase Admin SDK** - Client and server-side JWT authentication validation
* **localforage** - Advanced IndexedDB wrapper enabling asynchronous offline video storage
* **Framer Motion** - Production-ready fluid UI animation and transition library
* **Razorpay Node SDK** - Secure payment gateway integration for subscription tiers
* **@google/genai** - Google Gemini SDK enabling AI-driven mood recommendations

**Documentation:**

* **MDN Web Docs** - Comprehensive web technology reference (specifically utilized for IndexedDB protocols)
* **Socket.IO Documentation** - Official guides for socket multiplexing and dynamic room broadcasting
* **Firebase Documentation** - Official references for NoSQL Firestore modeling and Auth routing
* **Razorpay API Docs** - Integration guides for checkout tunnels and webhook signature verification

**Design Resources:**

* **TailwindCSS** - Primary utility-first CSS framework establishing the visual design system
* **Lucide React** - Comprehensive vector iconography library utilized throughout the application
* **TMDB API** - The Movie Database endpoints utilized for fetching high-resolution cinematic posters and metadata

**Hosting & Deployment:**

* **Firebase Firestore** – Primary NoSQL Database Hosting and Authorization
* **Cloudinary / YouTube** – Core Video Content Delivery Networks (CDN)
